    "q-89780": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89780",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt{3x+1}-2.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3x+1}-2=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3x+1}-2 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3x+1} & =2 \\\\ (\\sqrt{3x+1})^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ 3x+1 & =4 \\\\ 3x & =3 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3\\cdot 1+1}-2 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{4} & =2 \\\\ 2 & =2\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
