    "q-115389": {
      "dom_id": "step-q115389",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=3\\sqrt{1-x}+2.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n3\\sqrt{1-x}+2=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{1-x}+2 & =0 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{1-x} & =-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{1-x} & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no roots.",
